From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] standby: log DRAM save/restore progress (debug)

Deep suspend went silent after "the first time ddr standby" (printed
from the closed-source dramlib) and the console is re-bauded a few steps
later, so it was impossible to tell whether dram_power_save_process
returned. Print after the save call and around the resume-path restore
so the next run localises the hang:
  - "dram save done"    : the lib returned; hang is later (clk/system)
  - nothing             : hang inside dram_power_save_process
  - "wakeup: N" already : wake source fired (RTC path)
  - "ppu on"            : A55 power-up started after wake
  - "dram up enter/done": DRAM restore ran

Only builds into vendor-scp-debug (patches-debug/).

--- a/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
+++ b/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
@@ -431,11 +431,14 @@
 	}
 
 	dram_power_save_process((void *)(&dts_dram_para[0]));
+	LOG("dram save done\n");
 }
 
 static void dram_resume(void)
 {
+	LOG("dram up enter\n");
 	dram_power_up_process((void *)(&dts_dram_para[0]));
+	LOG("dram up done\n");
 
 	/* calc dram checksum */
 	if (standby_dram_crc_enable()) {
@@ -1377,6 +1380,7 @@
 	save_state_flag(REC_ESTANDBY | REC_ENTER_EXIT | 0x5);
 
 	ppu_resume();
+	LOG("ppu on\n");
 
 	clk_resume();
 	save_state_flag(REC_ESTANDBY | REC_ENTER_EXIT | 0x6);
